# Corpus unit pinn/C01 — justified (a measurement whose mandatory CQs are all met)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/pinn.yaml C01 (descriptive, cross_run_observation; corpus pin 62e9b54).
# Headline: near-zero training loss is necessary for accurate PINN solutions — pooled over the
# (PDE, optimizer, width, seed) sweep the final-loss-to-L2RE scatter is monotone, reaching
# L2RE ~ 1e-2 requires final loss ~ 1e-5 (order of magnitude, per PDE), and the loss~0/L2RE~1
# runs are near-constant trivial solutions (satisfy IC, fail BC) (E01, E06, Figure 2).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * cross_run_observation maps to the measurement family: conclusion
#     holds(low_loss_necessary_for_accuracy, pinn_benchmarks). The per-PDE threshold (~1e-5) and
#     the monotone-trend / trivial-solution content live in nl and refs.
#   * The measurement family carries NO variance_reported CQ; both of its mandatory CQs are
#     annotated met, so unlike the comparison/ablation gaps this claim clears the full bar and
#     is justified: instrument_validity (L2RE computed against ground truth on an independent
#     evaluation grid) and coverage (the sweep spans all optimizer combinations x widths
#     {50,100,200,400} x seeds, 41000 iterations each). The optional confound_control CQ is also
#     met — the loss~0/L2RE~1 runs are explained as trivial constant solutions, not scatter
#     noise — and is discharged.
#   * The optional "beyond three benchmark PDEs" CQ is unmet (convection/reaction/wave only);
#     omitted, no status effect, and absorbed by the binding (class-vs-tested scope).
#   * Coverage flag (kind-b wishlist, summary §3): the claim's core is a monotone functional
#     relationship between two continuous quantities (loss vs L2RE); no LARA construct expresses
#     graded functional dependence, so the atom is a per-PDE threshold surrogate — a concrete
#     v0.1-freeze construct candidate, noted here, not a lowering error.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact pinn at sha256:116d458ce7eb
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c01
  nl      = "Near-zero training loss is necessary for accurate PINN solutions: the pooled (PDE, optimizer, width, seed) loss-to-L2RE scatter is monotone, reaching L2RE ~ 1e-2 requires final loss ~ 1e-5 per PDE, and the loss ~ 0 / L2RE ~ 1 runs are near-constant trivial solutions (satisfy IC, fail BC)"
  formal  = holds(low_loss_necessary_for_accuracy, pinn_benchmarks)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the pooled monotone loss-to-L2RE observation over the full sweep, per run
# in the annotation and folded into refs.
leaf e1 : observes(e01, low_loss_necessary_for_accuracy, pinn_benchmarks)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Figure-2, logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-3, section-4, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N02]

leaf e2 : valid_instrument(low_loss_necessary_for_accuracy, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-2, logic/experiments.md#E06-Baselines]

leaf e3 : covers_scope(e01, pinn_benchmarks)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure]

leaf e4 : confounds_controlled(e01)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-4, logic/experiments.md#E06, Figure-2, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N02]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c01) by measurement(low_loss_necessary_for_accuracy, pinn_benchmarks, e01)
  discharge instrument_validity with e2
  discharge coverage            with e3
  discharge confound_control    with e4

status c01

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 alone, unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c01 -> justified (its complete support a1 is `in`; spec §8 aggregation)
